1
00:00:26,480 --> 00:00:29,440
This damn train doesn't even give us
a chance to catch our breath.

2
00:00:29,440 --> 00:00:31,600
Only the dead have plenty of time to rest.

3
00:00:31,600 --> 00:00:33,130
As long as we're breathing,

4
00:00:33,320 --> 00:00:35,320
we can definitely fight our way out.

5
00:00:35,720 --> 00:00:37,120
We will fight our way out.

6
00:00:38,240 --> 00:00:39,360
"Little White Boat."

7
00:00:39,360 --> 00:00:40,200
Listen,

8
00:00:40,560 --> 00:00:42,020
it's "Little White Boat."

9
00:00:42,800 --> 00:00:44,200
What "Little White Boat"?

10
00:00:44,200 --> 00:00:46,000
There's no sound outside at all.

11
00:00:53,000 --> 00:00:54,080
Station 2 cleared.

12
00:00:54,440 --> 00:00:55,680
Arrived at the new station.

13
00:00:55,680 --> 00:00:57,400
Station 3, Childhood Dream Amusement Park.

14
00:00:57,400 --> 00:00:58,320
Instance Background:

15
00:00:58,320 --> 00:01:00,320
Here lies the joy you longed
for most in childhood.

16
00:01:00,320 --> 00:01:01,880
Please collect three smiley face stamps

17
00:01:01,880 --> 00:01:02,840
to leave the park.

18
00:01:02,840 --> 00:01:03,760
An amusement park.

19
00:01:03,760 --> 00:01:05,239
It really is an amusement park.

20
00:01:05,239 --> 00:01:06,240
I'm finally here.

21
00:01:06,400 --> 00:01:07,560
Hurry, let's go in.

22
00:01:09,240 --> 00:01:11,570
His mental state is off.
Keep an eye on him.

23
00:01:29,039 --> 00:01:30,280
It really is an amusement park.

24
00:01:30,280 --> 00:01:31,680
Look at that elephant slide.

25
00:01:31,680 --> 00:01:32,360
Hurry up!

26
00:01:32,360 --> 00:01:34,759
My parents will come
pick me up before dark.

27
00:01:35,200 --> 00:01:36,240
Is he crazy?

28
00:01:36,560 --> 00:01:38,720
Where would his parents come from
in this hellhole?

29
00:01:38,720 --> 00:01:41,520
All the clocks are stopped at 5:30.

30
00:01:44,360 --> 00:01:47,160
5:30. Is that the closing time?

31
00:01:47,320 --> 00:01:50,050
What time did your parents say
they'd pick you up?

32
00:01:50,360 --> 00:01:53,520
5:30. They'll pick me up
after work at 5:30.

33
00:01:59,200 --> 00:02:00,600
It's a carousel!

34
00:02:00,600 --> 00:02:02,000
I want to ride this first.

35
00:02:03,120 --> 00:02:04,520
Come back! Don't run off!

36
00:02:37,480 --> 00:02:40,280
Are you my parents' colleagues?

37
00:02:40,520 --> 00:02:43,480
Did they ask you to celebrate
my birthday with me?

38
00:02:48,400 --> 00:02:49,120
Is this...

39
00:02:49,720 --> 00:02:50,920
Pang?

40
00:02:51,120 --> 00:02:52,600
First memory triggered:

41
00:02:52,640 --> 00:02:53,600
Sixth Birthday.

42
00:02:53,840 --> 00:02:54,880
Clearance Condition:

43
00:02:54,880 --> 00:02:57,440
Find the smiley face stamp
hidden in the memory.

44
00:02:57,440 --> 00:02:59,640
Stamp Location:
Bottom of the birthday cake.

45
00:02:59,640 --> 00:03:00,320
Hint:

46
00:03:00,320 --> 00:03:02,600
Do not forcefully interfere with
the actions of memory characters.

47
00:03:02,600 --> 00:03:03,920
This system is so sick.

48
00:03:04,120 --> 00:03:05,640
We have to snatch a birthday cake

49
00:03:05,640 --> 00:03:06,760
right in front of a six-year-old.

50
00:03:06,760 --> 00:03:07,560
It's okay.

51
00:03:07,560 --> 00:03:08,560
You guys eat the cake first.

52
00:03:08,560 --> 00:03:09,520
We'll blow out the candles together

53
00:03:09,520 --> 00:03:10,840
when my parents get back.

54
00:03:10,840 --> 00:03:13,700
They said they'd definitely
come back early today.

55
00:03:19,000 --> 00:03:21,160
Mom, Dad!

56
00:03:28,360 --> 00:03:30,800
Tell me, what are we going to do
about this month's rent?

57
00:03:30,800 --> 00:03:32,800
What can your meager salary even do?

58
00:03:33,400 --> 00:03:34,760
Not this again. Fine.

59
00:03:34,760 --> 00:03:35,800
It's all my fault.

60
00:03:35,800 --> 00:03:38,130
If you're so capable, go earn it yourself!

61
00:03:38,920 --> 00:03:40,400
Look at Mr. Wang next door.

62
00:03:40,400 --> 00:03:41,640
Look at what his wife wears.

63
00:03:41,640 --> 00:03:42,720
And look at what I wear.

64
00:03:42,720 --> 00:03:44,800
Marrying you was the
worst luck of my life.

65
00:03:44,800 --> 00:03:45,760
Are you done?

66
00:03:45,760 --> 00:03:47,040
All you care about is money!

67
00:03:47,040 --> 00:03:47,760
Mom,

68
00:03:47,760 --> 00:03:49,640
can we cut the cake?

69
00:03:50,000 --> 00:03:51,400
It's all because I had you!

70
00:03:51,400 --> 00:03:52,120
If it weren't for you,

71
00:03:52,120 --> 00:03:53,650
would I be living like this?

72
00:04:05,880 --> 00:04:08,720
Typical childhood trauma
from emotional neglect.

73
00:04:08,720 --> 00:04:10,880
The child learned to erase his presence

74
00:04:10,880 --> 00:04:12,940
under repeated pressure and denial,

75
00:04:13,000 --> 00:04:15,330
to avoid becoming the center of conflict.

76
00:04:33,200 --> 00:04:35,840
If you want to eat the cake, just eat it.

77
00:04:36,120 --> 00:04:37,640
It's your birthday cake.

78
00:04:37,760 --> 00:04:39,240
No need.

79
00:04:39,280 --> 00:04:42,520
We can eat it together
when Mom and Dad aren't mad anymore.

80
00:04:42,640 --> 00:04:43,920
If I'm a good boy,

81
00:04:43,920 --> 00:04:45,400
they won't fight.

82
00:04:45,800 --> 00:04:47,040
Please take the cake away.

83
00:04:47,040 --> 00:04:50,280
Acquire the stamp. Five minutes remaining.

84
00:04:55,240 --> 00:04:56,040
I'll do it.

85
00:04:57,480 --> 00:04:59,040
I dissect rotting flesh all day.

86
00:04:59,040 --> 00:05:01,170
I don't mind being hated a little more.

87
00:05:01,240 --> 00:05:03,840
Don't make yourself sound
like a born villain.

88
00:05:03,840 --> 00:05:05,360
You just can't stand seeing
others get their hands dirty,

89
00:05:05,360 --> 00:05:07,490
so you have to be the bastard yourself.

90
00:05:08,440 --> 00:05:11,360
Then this guilty conscience
is on both of us.

91
00:05:19,320 --> 00:05:21,600
It's okay, I'm not hungry.

92
00:05:21,600 --> 00:05:23,600
I don't have to eat.

93
00:05:32,960 --> 00:05:35,120
First smiley stamp acquired.

94
00:05:47,640 --> 00:05:50,040
Pang, are you okay?

95
00:05:50,520 --> 00:05:51,960
What happened to me just now?

96
00:05:51,960 --> 00:05:53,320
I think I had a dream.

97
00:05:53,600 --> 00:05:55,530
I dreamt that on my sixth birthday,

98
00:05:56,240 --> 00:05:57,880
my cake was taken away.

99
00:05:58,440 --> 00:05:59,700
Don't take it to heart.

100
00:06:00,000 --> 00:06:02,800
It's the only way to survive
in this damn game.

101
00:06:03,040 --> 00:06:04,970
Don't worry, I'm not that fragile.

102
00:06:05,120 --> 00:06:07,240
I've seen too much of the ugly,
rotting side of human nature.

103
00:06:07,240 --> 00:06:08,280
I'm numb to it.

104
00:06:10,800 --> 00:06:13,060
Let's go. We still have two stamps to get.

105
00:06:43,400 --> 00:06:46,520
It's a test paper.
That's his torn test paper.

106
00:06:46,600 --> 00:06:49,800
Is the clearance condition
to piece this paper together

107
00:06:49,800 --> 00:06:50,800
to find the stamp?

108
00:06:51,200 --> 00:06:55,130
The condition is that we have to
piece it together right in front of him.

109
00:07:03,240 --> 00:07:03,760
Dad,

110
00:07:03,760 --> 00:07:05,120
I got a 99.

111
00:07:05,120 --> 00:07:06,240
First in the class.

112
00:07:09,400 --> 00:07:10,440
Ninety-nine?

113
00:07:11,320 --> 00:07:13,180
Where did you lose that one point?

114
00:07:14,040 --> 00:07:16,920
I wrote one character wrong
in the last question.

115
00:07:18,520 --> 00:07:20,560
Wrote it wrong? Are you blind?

116
00:07:20,600 --> 00:07:22,320
How could you make such a simple mistake?

117
00:07:22,320 --> 00:07:24,760
Kneel. Kneel until you figure it out.

118
00:07:30,640 --> 00:07:31,840
We can't piece it together anymore.

119
00:07:31,840 --> 00:07:33,800
Every time we touch these pieces,

120
00:07:33,800 --> 00:07:35,880
he has to relive the pain of being beaten.

121
00:07:35,880 --> 00:07:38,800
Calm down. If we don't finish it,
we can't get the stamp,

122
00:07:38,800 --> 00:07:39,860
and no one gets out.

123
00:07:47,360 --> 00:07:49,560
I was wrong. Dad, I was wrong.

124
00:07:49,560 --> 00:07:52,760
I'll definitely get a 100 next time.
Please don't tear it.

125
00:08:01,800 --> 00:08:03,080
You did nothing wrong.

126
00:08:03,080 --> 00:08:04,560
A 99 is great.

127
00:08:04,560 --> 00:08:05,760
You did nothing wrong.
